<title>USA: Duke shuts 1,129 MW S.C. nuclear unit--NRC.</title>
<headline>Duke shuts 1,129 MW S.C. nuclear unit--NRC.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duke Power Co on Monday shut its 1,129 megawatt (MW) Catawba 1 nuclear reactor in Clover, South Carolina, the U.S. Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Tuesday in its daily plant status report.  </p>
<p>The adjacent Catawba 2 unit, with an identical generating capacity, is operating at full power, the NRC report said.</p>
<p>((New York Power Desk 212-859-1624))</p>
